  "query_preview": "(Friday through Next Week)\nThe upper-level pattern shifts Friday as an expansive ridge \ncentered near the Four Corners builds into the Great Plains. A \nstalled surface front over southern Illinois may support \nlingering morning showers, but the trend for central Illinois \nhas been drier as surface ridging builds in from the north. \nHighs will reach the mid-80s with dew points in the mid-70s \nmaintaining a humid air mass. Heat will intensify through the \nweekend in response to the expanding upper ridge, with triple- \ndigit heat indices possible by Sunday and Monday as temperatures\nclimb into the upper 80s to lower 90s. The chance for reaching \nand exceeding 100F heat index Sunday is around 40% across \nportions of the lower Illinois River Valley (southwest of Havana\nto Springfield) and 40% south of a Canton to Casey line Monday.\n\nA \"Ring of Fire\" pattern will dominate this weekend through early\nnext week, with nocturnal MCS activity riding the periphery of \nthe ridge. While there is a chance for storms in the forecast each\nnight, Saturday night appears most favorable for widespread \nconvection across central Illinois as the instability gradient \ndrapes overhead. By Monday, the ridge begins to break down, \nallowing an effective frontal boundary to gradually slide back \nsouth through the week. This will initiate a gradual cooling \ntrend, with highs in the 90s Monday yielding to the mid-80s by \nThursday as PoPs trend southward with the advancing boundary.",
